-- The Black Morass (map 269): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent c4eda29
-- (dungeons/black_morass.json, status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)') with the options of the header of 20261017130000:
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 269 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev c4eda29 \
--     --stamp 20261024020900 --out <dir> black_morass
-- Stacks on 20261023220000. The draft this replaces was never merged or applied anywhere; this file is the first export of the plan.
-- NO ROW IS HAND-SET: the plan file is the source; the census fixes over the generated skeleton are in
-- ~/TortoiseBots-audit/PREP-BLACK-MORASS-2026-10-24.md ("Fixes applied"). In short:
--   * critters: the 28 Snakes (entry 2914, faction 190, level 1, 9 hp) were pack members in 28 draft groups, 26 of them pulls of
--     nothing but a snake; they are out of every group and no pull of one is left.
--   * split packs: the Time Anomaly 50106 and the Echo of Time 61318 in the z -98 cave (7.7 yd apart) were two rows for one pack,
--     and the Riftguard 65101 and four Dragonspawn 65100 at y 6720 (8-13 yd) two rows for another; each pair is one group now.
--   * Epochronos' guard: the Time Anomaly 50106 at -1450.10 6967.23 -14.3097 stood 18.9 yd from Epochronos (detection 20). It is the
--     leg's last pull now, right before the boss, so the boss joins that one fight and not a mid-leg one.
--   * patrols: five spawns walk creature_movement paths (65100 guid 2567942, 237 yd ~95 s; 65101 2567943, 190 yd ~76 s; 65101
--     2567944, 184 yd ~74 s; 61318 2574761, 319 yd ~128 s; 61318 2574775, 431 yd ~172 s). Every group whose stand is within 25 yd
--     of a path carries that patrol block (entries, path, estimated period).
--   * radii: each pull row is a single point for the run leader, so a group's radius is the farthest member from the group's centre
--     plus that member's wander plus 1 yd: 2 for a lone stationary spawn, 6 for a 5 yd wanderer, 9-15.4 for the merged packs. All
--     positions are exact spawn rows; the plan check's pack overlap counts 0.
--   * route: the leg order is the shortest of the 24 permutations (7,852 yd from the entrance; the next best is +532); within each leg
--     the groups are a 3-D 2-opt from the leg's start to its boss (5,797->4,940, 1,522->1,347, 3,321->2,789, 1,900->1,751 yd; vertical
--     travel 270->267, 53->55, 651->593, 491->452).
-- 4 legs, 522 steps, 527 rows (131 + 23 + 66 + 32 pulls; bosses in leg order 65125 Antnormi, 50105 Medivh, 65116 Time-Lord
-- Epochronos, 65113 Chronar; no boss.first). Plan check (turtle-agent plan-check, map 269 mmaps): 4 of 301 points fail, all 'too far' look
-- points (leg 1 group 18; leg 2 groups 5, 19, 57), 25 estimated-patrol-period warnings and 247 run-leader hop warnings (a pull or boss
-- 50-100+ yd from the move row before it). Six approach hops could not be cut at all (leg 3 steps 2, 3, 5, 15, 18, 22: no complete
-- navmesh route, the nearest reachable point 12.6-90.3 yd from the pack).
--
-- WHAT THE RUN LEADER CANNOT DO (issue #984: nothing is dropped silently). Not in these rows:
--   * no_cc 50106,61316,61317,61318,61575,65100,65101,65102,65103,65105,65110,65111,65112,65122,65124 (there is no such column in
--     ai_dungeon_plan): no trash in the instance is humanoid, so no Polymorph lands; cc_priority and cc_always are empty, and the run
--     leader's crowd control picks from those two only.
--   * fleers: empty for a reason. No creature script and no EventAI row in the instance flees at low health (no Flee, no command 47).
--   * patrol: each pull's patrol block is for the agent's driver; the run leader's rows carry no patrol and it pulls where the pack
--     stands when it arrives. Mossheart 65124, Medivh 50105 and the Bronze Defenders 65126/65128 have movement_type 2 but no movement
--     rows, so no block could be written for them.
--   * floors: the map is stacked (the cave column z -165..+56 and the lower hall z -230..-122 hold packs above and below each other).
--     Aggro is 3-D, so they are not pull members, but the route between floors is the mapping walk's first item: the six uncut
--     approach hops above and the 247 hop warnings.
--   * Medivh 50105 is FACTION 35 (friendly to the party), has no script and 1,024,000 hp: the leg 1 boss row is a destination
--     marker. The run leader's boss step reads 'boss is friendly to this party: left alone' and the leg advances.
--   * Epochronos 65116 at 50 % banishes itself and summons one Echo (65117 Lich King / 65118 Kael'thas / 65119 Vashj) that must die
--     before it unbanishes; no plan field names a summoned add. Rotmaw 65122's Consume (a player shrunk and helpless for 15.5 s) and
--     the Whelp 65103's mana drain are fight mechanics the rows cannot carry.
--   * the entrance (trigger 1632, portal map 1 -8799.19 -4115.16 -199.999, required level 58), level_band 59-60 and
--     hire_composition: the run leader starts inside the instance and leads the bound party as it is.

-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- black_morass: map 269, 4 legs, 522 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'black_morass';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'black_morass';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'black_morass';


-- The dashboard's boss table: rank and name for this plan's bosses (the step rows cannot carry creature_template's data).
-- Same pattern as 20261021114931_world.sql. Entry-scoped so another plan's map-269 rows would survive; no map-269 boss row
-- exists on this branch yet.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (269) AND `entry` IN (65125, 50105, 65116, 65113);
